    {
      "source": "TEKS0043130.jpg",
      "observer": "project owner",
      "observation": "Seventh die bond wire counted from the bottom on the right side (third in the separated upper-half group) reaches the sixth carrier finger counted from the top. The corresponding die pad in figure3.5 is VDD.",
      "interpretation": "With the colour photo notch right and a symmetric split of carrier fingers into the two 20-pin banks, this finger is the first of the upper/first DIP bank, hence candidate pin1.",
      "assistant_review": "Enlarged right-side crop is consistent with a mid-side wire landing. All fine endpoints and buried external-lead routes are not independently resolved. Corner-finger counting must be kept explicit when comparing ordinals.",
      "status": "Owner-traced bond supports VDD=1 independently of connector ordering; external mapping still uses the symmetric-carrier assumption."
    },
    {
      "source": "TEKS0043130.jpg",
      "observer": "project owner",
      "observation": "Sixth carrier finger counted from the bottom on the left side (including the corner in the count) reaches the upper of a close pair of die pads. A second close pair follows after a short gap.",
      "interpretation": "For the notch-right colour view and symmetric bank split, the finger is candidate pin21. The first pair matches VSS and the unlabeled candidate LOUT pad after rotating figure3.5 by 180 degrees; the following pair matches AB0/AB1.",
      "assistant_review": "The enlarged left-side crop shows the relevant bonds/pad grouping. Fine endpoints are not all independently resolved. The page35 pattern has VSS/neighbor and AB0/AB1 close pairs in the stated rotated orientation.",
      "status": "Owner-traced bond supports VSS=21 independently of connector ordering, under the existing orientation/carrier assumptions."
    }
  ],
